# Testing Rules

- The core logic MUST be testable.
- `reverseString(str)` must remain a pure function.
- Include basic unit tests inside `script.js` using simple assertion checks.
- Do not use external testing frameworks.
- Provide a small test runner function executed on load.

Minimum required test cases:
- "AI4Devs" -> "sveD4IA"
- "" -> ""
- "a" -> "a"
- "hola mundo" -> "odnum aloh"
- "😀a" -> "a😀"

If any test fails, log a clear error in the console.